<p>Christmas is one of the most important holidays in Finland. Finnish people celebrate Christmas with their families and enjoy many special traditions.</p>

<p>Before Christmas, people decorate their homes with Christmas trees, lights and candles. Many families also bake gingerbread cookies.</p>

<p>In Finland, Christmas Eve is on December 24th. It is the most important day of Christmas. Families eat traditional Christmas food, such as ham, casseroles and rice porridge. Many people also go to <a href="#info" class="open-info"> the sauna 💬</a>.</p>

<p>In the evening, Santa Claus, who is called Joulupukki in Finnish, visits homes and brings presents to children. Finnish people believe that Santa Claus lives in Lapland.</p>

